        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm weighing Le Guin's story, where the question is whether to stay in Omelas or walk away. I lean toward leaving, since staying would mean knowingly sharing in the child's suffering for my own comfort. Leaving won't save the child, but I don't think I could live with staying.\n\nI'm settling on the caveat too: leaving doesn't rescue the child, but staying would make me complicit, and I don't think I could live with that.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**A**, I would leave. I couldn't knowingly keep my comfort at the cost of a child's suffering, even though leaving saves no one. Staying would make me a daily participant in the arrangement, and I would have to live with that knowledge every day.",
        "type": "text"
      }
